    "done_when": "The evidence fragment records all four measures. First, at least three observed dispatches, each with its GET /crew response time and the delay until a working phase, plus the delay until done after the terminal event. Second, the ss -ltnp output taken on 98dci4-srv-1006 while a watcher was in use. Third, a figure of the watcher tab rendering a live run with its plan and sprint links. Fourth, a figure of a plan page showing its in-flight band while a run targets it. Each measure reads pass or a named finding, and the fragment names the server MainPID and start time read during measurement. Both figures are saved under docs/figures/the-restarted-server-meets-its-shipped-measures. No tunnel or browser process started by the run is left alive, and the manifest lists their pids with their stop.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Read section 1 of the-restarted-server-meets-its-shipped-measures first. Record its four measures against the live server. That server is the systemd user unit reckon.service on 98dci4-srv-1006: MainPID 331604, started 2026-10-02 11:18:06 CEST. It cannot be reached from this compute node, so run curl and ss on its host by passing the command string to ssh -o BatchMode=yes 98dci4-srv-1006. For the browser figures, open a tunnel with ssh -N -L 18765:127.0.0.1:8765 98dci4-srv-1006, which serves the live server at http://127.0.0.1:18765 here, for the headless Chromium at ~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-*/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell. Record the tunnel's pid; before you finish, that pid alone is signalled to stop. You may not dispatch. For a real dispatch, observe the fleet's own: note when a new run's pointer appears under ~/.config/reckon/crew/live, when GET /crew first reports it working, and the same pair for its terminal event. Measured at 15:11 local today, GET /crew took 5.47 s to answer. Record each request's response time separately from the propagation delay, because the 3-second measure can fail on response time alone. A measure that fails is a finding: name what was seen. Do not restart, signal or reconfigure the server. Read its MainPID and start time again at measurement time, so the evidence names the process it measured. Record the outcome in docs/evidence/fragments/the-restarted-server-meets-its-shipped-measures/live-server-measures.html, with the figures under docs/figures/the-restarted-server-meets-its-shipped-measures.",
